llama.cpp v0.5.0 (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, release build b11146, commit
7fe450e19305b828c199d602c23a8337aaa1f03b)

Ollaya runs GGUF models on llama.cpp. The libraries in lib/ollaya/llama, and libggml-cuda.so in
the CUDA package's lib/ollaya/cuda_v13, are ggml-org's own release build of llama.cpp v0.5.0,
unmodified: libllama, libmtmd, libggml, libggml-base and the ggml backends. They are licensed under the
MIT license, and contain the components below, whose license texts follow. None of these files is
covered by Ollaya's Apache-2.0 license.

  llama.cpp and ggml    MIT    The ggml authors
  llamafile sgemm       MIT    Mozilla Foundation (in the CPU backends)
  libmtmd dependencies        See the additional notices below

libggml-cuda.so, in the CUDA package, was compiled by ggml-org with the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit 13.4 and
contains code generated from its headers (CCCL: CUB, Thrust and libcu++, Apache License 2.0 with LLVM
Exceptions, https://github.com/NVIDIA/cccl). It runs with the NVIDIA libraries in the same directory.

